course: dictionary
lesson: 11035
title: Strengths and weaknesses
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A weakness is a part of something, or of someone, that is not strong or good enough yet. «Spelling is my weakness» means spelling is the part I need to practise most. Knowing your weaknesses helps you know what to work on.
explain: Weakness can also mean that your body has little strength. «Weakness in her legs» means her legs feel too weak to hold her up well. In health lessons, sudden weakness is a sign to tell an adult straight away.
explain: Check the context to find which meaning fits. «Telling a trusted adult is not weakness; it brings in someone with the power to stop the trouble.» Here the sentence says asking for help is not weakness, so weakness must mean something to be ashamed of, and the sentence says it is not.
fact: Weakness can mean: not being strong in the body; a part that is not good enough; or a liking you find hard to resist.
fact: «A weakness for chocolate» means you like chocolate so much that it is hard to say no to it.
fact: «Strengths and weaknesses» means the good things you can do and the things you need to practise.
fact: In stories, heroes and villains often have a weakness, like Superman and kryptonite, or Achilles and his heel.
fact: Weakness is uncountable when it means the state of being weak, but a weakness (weaknesses in the plural) is a particular fault or gap.
exercise: «Spelling is my weakness.» What does weakness mean here? | *A part I am not good at yet | Feeling very strong and brave | A loud noise in the classroom | A kind of sweet treat
exercise: «A weakness for chocolate» means what? | You make chocolate in a factory | *You like chocolate so much it is hard to resist | You are allergic to all sweets | You have never tasted chocolate
exercise: «Telling a trusted adult is not weakness.» What does this sentence tell you? | Weakness means telling jokes | Only grown-ups are allowed to tell secrets | Adults are always weak | *Asking for help is nothing to be ashamed of
test: In the phrase «strengths and weaknesses», what are the weaknesses? | *Things you need to practise and get better at | Things you have lost at school | Things that are coloured blue | Things you are best at and love doing
test: In many stories, what do heroes and villains often have? | A magic hat that never comes off | A pet dragon | *A weakness that can be used against them | Two names and a secret cave
exam: «Ethical hackers are hired to test systems and report weaknesses.» What does weaknesses mean here? | Good jokes that make people laugh | Rules for playing football | Happy days when the system works | *Places in a system that could be broken into
